#C) Restoring deleted commits

# git reflog

---

    Scenario 1: Recover after git reset --hard
    Original history
    A ---- B ---- C (HEAD)
    git reset --hard A
    A (HEAD)
    You panic because B and C disappeared.
    git reflog
    HEAD@{0}: reset: moving to A
    HEAD@{1}: commit: C
    HEAD@{2}: commit: B

    Recover:
    git reset --hard HEAD@{1}
    or
    git reset --hard <hash-of-C>

    History is restored:
    A ---- B ---- C

---

    Scenario 2: Recover a deleted branch

    Suppose

    main
    A ---- B

    feature
        \
        C ---- D

    You delete feature

    git branch -D feature

    The branch disappears. But

    git reflog

    may contain

    checkout: moving from feature to main
    commit: D
    commit: C

    Now recreate it

    git branch feature <hash-of-D>

    Recovered.

